#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064013 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064030 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7558fff-d697-5dda-879e-5b66e4da6fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289107} {:answer/id #uuid "0337ec50-1281-5f53-87d6-01d2705a10f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289108} {:answer/id #uuid "bddc3cf2-3f22-5caf-93ac-23307c7115ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289109} {:answer/id #uuid "93450f80-7305-5aec-b8ec-a22229ad2662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289110} {:answer/id #uuid "6259b2e9-3e7b-59b7-bfb0-173616ef23cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bddc3cf2-3f22-5caf-93ac-23307c7115ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289109} :answer-field/id #uuid "741db9be-5b9b-54e5-9fe9-b7b974d0dd70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2f0b068-41b8-5842-8ef3-240b1ca8e48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114287" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "654b3963-72be-5d2d-ab21-468291cae36b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289128} {:answer/id #uuid "9c08afd9-7502-5e45-bcae-5d34da2f52b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289129} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fb474c-7e53-5437-9a65-388ead62564c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289130} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b781ec-938b-5f02-8e23-aac6bda548c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289131} {:answer/id #uuid "20e24aae-7294-5f43-b360-89d0d52fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e24aae-7294-5f43-b360-89d0d52fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289132} :answer-field/id #uuid "097e307a-baf0-562a-a260-70b760dce7bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e39f59c6-1dff-56e6-932b-2ba7bba5a751" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b33630c-ecb5-56f2-ac14-1b6e8f4d8588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289170} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e0ce0e-76dc-5a7d-997d-67b939ee60fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289171} {:answer/id #uuid "8b16bd54-1ca7-5f2f-b410-221a5b572f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289172} {:answer/id #uuid "45a33943-b861-59c1-89c3-26eb11f72abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289173} {:answer/id #uuid "ad468f28-f450-5fa3-868d-b9834bd738d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b16bd54-1ca7-5f2f-b410-221a5b572f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289172} :answer-field/id #uuid "f875e6b9-8981-5816-a243-dbaaacb5933a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fee3246-3b94-5446-856c-0c95a1862f47" :question/math-academy-id "q-2420" :question/problem "$\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{5}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={5}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{{5}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
